  "articleSummary": "The article argues that security agents should be evaluated by **model routing** rather than static rankings, because agent performance depends on matching models to specific subtasks (discovery, planning, tool use, integration) under cost and latency constraints. Using a product-specific eval suite for ExploitHunter.app, it compares eight model routes on a hard Juice Shop task; cheaper models like Kimi K3 and GPT-5.6 Luna can match or exceed premium models (e.g., Claude Opus) on score while being far cheaper, revealing a cost-quality frontier that makes leaderboard thinking misleading. The tone is analytical with a critical edge toward “winner” benchmarks, framing the problem as “a routing problem, not a leaderboard problem.” The intended audience is engineers building security agents.",
